Print "=== Lists Demo ===".
Print "Integer list [10, 20, 30]:".
a list called 'number list' is [10, 20, 30].
For each number in 'number list',
  print the number.
print "".

(Access specific elements by index - 1-indexed like natural English)
Print "Second element of numbers: ".
Print element 2 of 'number list'.

Print "Boolean list [true, true, false]:".
a list called answers is [true, true, false].
For each answer in answers,
  print the answer.
print "".

Print "First element: ".
Print answers's first.

Print "Last element: ".
Print answers's last.

print answers's size.

print "You should see an error below".
(Reading past the end is what raises the error caught on the next line)
a boolean called 'answer out of range' is element 100 of answers.
On error print "Cannot access element 100 - out of bounds!".

Print "Word list [\"hello\", \"world\"]:".
a list called words is ["hello", "world"].
For each word in words,
  print the word.
print "".

Print "Done!".
